string regexPattern = @"^" + prefix + @".*";
Regex compiledRegexPattern = new Regex(regexPattern);
```

In all examples above, the `prefix` is concatenated to the beginning of the regular expression pattern using the appropriate syntax for each language. The `.*` wildcard character matches any character (except a newline) between zero and unlimited times, allowing the rest of the string to be matched after the prefix.

